 "answer": "Based on the context provided, promptfoo requires that any provider used must have legitimate access to the models they serve. This means the provider must either own the models, have licenses from the users, or access the models through a first-party API, partner agreement, or reseller agreement. For IBM-hosted models, you would need to ensure that you have a provider that meets these criteria and has access to IBM's models.\n\nThe documents do not specify a particular promptfoo provider for IBM-hosted models. To find an appropriate provider, you should:\n\n1. Verify if there is an existing promptfoo provider that has a partnership or agreement with IBM to access their models.\n2. Check IBM's own offerings or APIs that could be integrated with promptfoo.\n3. Contact IBM to inquire about any available APIs or partnerships that could be utilized with promptfoo.\n\nIf no such provider is available, you may need to configure a new provider that can interface with IBM's models, ensuring compliance with promptfoo's requirements for legitimate model access and accountable ownership.",
